{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Brainstorm complete and approved (2026-09-03).\n\nThe design is decomposed into four dependency-ordered executable tasks:\n1. `forcible-diminished-lamb` — plan-review Terraform structural grounding vertical slice.\n2. `salmon-abominable-pupa` — code-review IaC grounding; depends on S1.\n3. `depraved-classless-rooster` — local/registry source probing; depends on S2.\n4. `schematic-gleesome-ballpython` — optional `terraform-config-inspect` corroboration; depends on S3.\n\nThe leaves are typed `task` (correcting the earlier childless-`story` authoring mismatch). `next_batch(yaw-quota-wraith)` now returns S1 alone. S1 has a current signed plan-review PASS (job `1788478341336192000-84aea946da9343fba8b3508cb2d89626`, verified at `ebbcd7a030d6029216127c83fb43c415117af366`). The blocked descendants were intentionally not reviewed; review each only after its predecessor closes.\n\nApproved boundary:\n- Terraform support is isolated behind the `grounding-terraform` extra with exact direct dependency `python-hcl2==8.1.3`; core and non-Terraform projects gain no Terraform-specific dependency or tools.\n- The feature grounds LLM-generated IaC findings for Terraform-routed Pass 1 and gives Pass 2 a fresh, independent re-grounding session. It does not duplicate mechanical Terraform validation suited to CI.\n- Whole affected-module indexing includes sibling files, literal in-repo child modules, and in-repo reverse callers so file-scoped evidence cannot silently misstate module-wide symbols.\n- Rebar never executes Terraform, OpenTofu, providers, repository plugins/config, TFLint, Trivy, tfparse, terraform-ls, or terraform-docs. The only optional executable is `terraform-config-inspect`, run under the separately specified copied-snapshot, hardened subprocess contract.\n- V1 reads local content already available in the client project and treats remote sources as metadata only. Remote content fetch using ambient credentials is approved as a documented future extension if demand justifies it. Every access failure abstains; 401/403/404 never prove nonexistence.\n- Limits are 64 modules, 5,000 files, 32 MiB, and 60 seconds. A limit or safety failure returns one abstention and no partial facts.\n\nParser evidence correction: an isolated exact-wheel probe showed that serialized `SerializationOptions(with_meta=True)` does not provide the planned source ranges. The implementation contract now uses public `hcl2.parses_to_tree(text)` and Lark `Tree.meta`, with `propagate_positions=True` confirmed upstream. Serialized metadata is explicitly not an oracle.\n\nNo production code was changed or claimed during brainstorming."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788480122415591227,"uuid":"158b9898-4f8d-4526-9c5c-219e96983327"}